Melee-NX-NetPlay 0.4.4 (patches/net-0005), as melee-unlocked does them (its slippi_online.cpp search_away / kept_search and
handle of command 0xED, port/runtime/abi/mu_pick_preview.h):
- Play while you search: a kept search (slippi::online::keep_search) goes on through the game's own cleanup commands while the
  player plays offline (the frontend's search module decides when; nothing changes unless the player chose it).
- search_info(): the search's state, mode, the locked-in fighter, whether the others locked in, elapsed time, error and
  opponent, for that module (and the warm-up room, which keeps a Direct or Teams connection the same way).
- Live pick previews between two Melee-NX-NetPlay builds: the build message goes to version 2 with flag 0x04 (this build reads
  pick previews) and NP_MSG_NX_PICK (0xD1) carries melee-unlocked's pick preview bytes; command 0xED answers the game's online
  character select (op 0 send, op 1 read). Against Slippi Dolphin or melee-unlocked nothing is sent and every slot reads empty.
- frame_trace(): the last online frame's wait, time sync halt or advance and time sync offset (the session trace and the network
  overlay).
Applied by ../net_sources.sh after net-0004; mu_pick_preview.h is copied from the fetched tree there. port/ is unchanged.
